# Line endings: every text file is stored with LF and checked out with LF
# on every platform, also on Windows with core.autocrlf=true. The shell
# scripts (build.sh, tools/*.sh) only run with LF, and the expected outputs
# of the tests (*.out, tests/rosetta/results.tsv) are compared byte for byte
# with the output of the programs, which ends its lines with LF. A source
# with CR LF would also shift the columns in the compiler's messages.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.tex linguist-documentation
*.html linguist-documentation

# Binary files: never converted and never diffed as text.
*.jar   binary
*.class binary
*.m68   binary
*.vsix  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.tgz   binary
